        "ggRg8OT95fP_text": "<p>|</p>",
        "ggSJnR7TCHY_text": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">Brushing sessions that take 10 minutes and end in a fight get skipped. And skipped sessions are why the buildup comes back. A routine you'll actually do every day beats a thorough one you do twice a month. FreshWipes make it easy.</span></p>",
        "ggU88rVCxj6_text": "<p><strong>FREE</strong> Shipping</p>",
        "ggVmccshQLH_text": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">Most owners say the same thing: their dog just sat there. No fight. No drama. And after that first calm session, the next one was easier. Then the next. Within a week it's just part of the routine. That's what consistent daily care actually looks like. Not a battle. Just 30 seconds.</span></p>",
        "ggWzuUC7vfc_srcSet_desktop_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0735/4833/3323/files/hf_20260501_074227_f47ab5d3-dc84-43df-a7e3-3e6e5010673d.png",
        "ggWzuUC7vfc_srcSet_mobile_src": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0735/4833/3323/files/hf_20260501_064955_ad275b98-8abb-4c11-a188-861084ff14a3.png",
        "ggXZRKsVZv-_text": "<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;\">Toothbrush bristles press into gum tissue. If there's any early inflammation which there usually is when buildup has been going on a while and that pressure hurts. The soft textured wipe cleans without pressing. To your dog, it feels like a rub, not a scrape.</span></p>",
        "ggZS4xi3GZP_dayLabel": "Days",
